<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#xuanming-calendar">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xuanming calendar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/822">822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Senmyō calendar, Senmyō-reki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xuanming calendar was an astronomical calendar compiled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> and adopted in 822. It reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> with an embassy from Balhae and was introduced there in 862 as the Senmyō calendar, which Japan then used, without official revision, for more than 800 years, until it was replaced by the Jōkyō calendar in 1685.</p></div>
